    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0392" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1248½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Hoover
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-06">July 6, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I am sending you herewith a
                    stenographic record of my talk yesterday with Norman
                        Davis,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d184-f1"/> which I summarized to you
                    at Cabinet Meeting. It is so interesting that I thought you would like to read
                    it in full. As you will see, there is still a possibility of something
                    unpleasant coming out either in the House of Commons or in Simon’s speech; but in general what was a very
                    awkward matter is smoothing down into pretty good shape.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
